# Screen Display — Sidebar rule

When account preference `mode` is `sidebar`:

- Force **preferred + active** local/session storage to `sidebar` together (color/tone too).
- Apply Sidebar on **every desktop page** (boot, body class, left rail, menu hydrate, login apply).
- Never leave Classic on desktop after server/login says Sidebar.
- Login must load prefs by the **signed-in user id**, never the previous request cookie.

Phone/tablet (`max-width: 900px`):

- Keep the **existing** narrow mobile shell (top bar / home drawer). Do not redesign or force the desktop left rail on narrow viewports.
- Still keep `mode = sidebar` so mobile shell stays available; do not fall back to Classic.

```js
// ❌ BAD — Sidebar preferred but active/classic left on another page
writePreferredMode('sidebar');
// active left as classic

// ✅ GOOD
forceSidebarEverywhere(color, tone); // preferred + active both sidebar
```
